cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Videoanálise Móvel"
abstract: >-
  Videoanálise Móvel is a web application for frame-by-frame video analysis on
  Android phones, for introductory physics labs. Students record an experiment
  with the phone's camera, calibrate the scale and the axes, mark the position
  of each object by hand or with automatic tracking, and export t, x, y as CSV
  in the format of Tracker. Everything runs in the browser, and the video
  never leaves the device.
authors:
  - given-names: "Victor Abath"
    family-names: "Silva"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AbathVictor/Physics-Mobile-Track"
url: "https://abathvictor.github.io/Physics-Mobile-Track/"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - physics education
  - video analysis
  - motion tracking
  - kinematics
  - experimental physics
  - mobile learning
  - progressive web app
